# ============================================================
# DAWNTRADER — Git Attributes
# No LFS tracking — large runtime data is excluded via .gitignore
# ============================================================
infra/helsinki/*.sh text eol=lf
# Comms-infra Discord bridges deploy to Linux (Helsinki). Force LF so a Windows-authored
# edit can't ship CRLF into a shebang / systemd unit and break execution (B-DISCORD-INBOUND-LIVENESS).
comms-infra/discord/** text eol=lf

# B-DEPLOY-LOCK (#649): ALL shell scripts ship LF — a CRLF working copy broke
# dt-deploy.sh's shebang on staging (exit 127). Same class as the helsinki rule.
*.sh text eol=lf

# B-CROSS-SESSION-BLEED (#753): AN ARCHIVE THAT NORMALISES IS NOT AN ARCHIVE.
# `core.autocrlf` rewrote two deleted CRLF-stored scripts to LF on `git add`, so the
# .removed copies no longer matched the blobs they were preserving — and CRLF-vs-LF was
# the exact property whose loss made the deletion census wrong in the first place.
# `-text` disables all EOL conversion here so a deleted file is archived as it WAS.
# ⚠ SCOPED TO THESE THREE, DELIBERATELY. A directory-wide `-text` re-normalised all 45
# pre-existing .removed files at once - rewriting OTHER batches' archives under my name,
# which is rule 25.c exactly: the path is right and the content is not mine to change.
1-system-manual/_archive/deleted-code/REPLIT_PUSH_SCRIPT*.removed -text
